  "measure": "lw: sound power by the documentation's eq. (2)-(4): each microphone's pressure squared through the fast time weighting (125 ms), averaged over the whole recording, the microphones' energetic mean, + 10 log10(54.63 m^2); it reproduces 3_Audio_Features.csv's \"SoundPower in dB\" for all 156 harp recordings within 0.005 dB (csv: the CSV's value; the plain mean square without the weighting differs by up to 0.65 dB at pp, the fast maximum by 6.8 dB on average). energy = lw + 10 log10(lengthS): dB re 1 pW s, independent of where the recording was cut (decaying tones have no steady part: SteadyPart [0 0]); onsetS: the fast envelope's first crossing of its peak - 30 dB",
  "harp": "Double action harp modern, every note at pp and ff (MIDI pitch keys)",
  "timpani": "Pedal timpani and Timpani, D2 only (the database has no other pitch); the CSV has no timpani. Series v1 .. v4 by mallet and beating spot, each \"6 dynamics\" (or 3 / 4) in rising order, the markings not named"
